{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And every woman who has known a man.</b> Eligible for intercourse, even if she was not intercourse'd — and they passed them before the frontal plate, and her who is eligible for intercourse, her face turns green (Yevamot 60a)." "<b>Kill.</b> Why did he go back and say it? To break up the matter — the words of Rabbi Yishmael: for if I read ״kill every male among the little ones and every woman who has known a man and every little one among the women, etc.,״ I do not know whether to kill with the males or to keep alive with the little ones; therefore ״kill״ was said."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:25.017827764Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}